Argument Against Measure F
Vote NO on Measure F. Defend the EXISTING term limits.
In 2018, an overwhelming 83% of Lake Forest voters delivered a mandate:
we passed a measure to establish strict lifetime term limits of two four-year terms for Lake Forest City Council Members.
Now, to cling to power and continue to get their City pay, Councilmembers
Scott Voigts and Mark Tettemer, who are set to be termed out this year,
have placed a deceptive new measure on the ballot. Their goal is to
replace the existing term limits with the new Measure F. They’re trying to
trick you by framing their new measure as “introducing” term limits.
Councilmembers Voigts and Tettemer have each already served a total
of 16 years on the City Council: 8 Years before we had Term Limits and 8
years after Term Limits passed in 2018.
Their new measure, if passed, will replace the current term limits and
allow them to serve two additional terms, take a break, and then come
back for another two terms. If their new measure passes, these two
politicians will end up controlling Lake Forest politics and its hundreds of
millions of dollars for 32 out of 36 years. That isn’t a limit -- that’s a career,
and, in their case, a lucrative one.
Defend the EXISTING true term limits. Vote NO on Measure F.
s/ James (Jim) Gardner
Former Lake Forest Mayor and City Councilmember
